.TH "SVGTEXTPATHELEMENT" "3JS" "July 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGTextPathElement \- SVGTextPathElement
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]SVGTextPathElement\f[B]\f[R] interface corresponds to the
\f[CR]<textPath>\f[R] element.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]This interface also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]SVGTextContentElement\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.href\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedString\f[R] corresponding to the \f[CR]href\f[R] or
\f[CR]xlink:href\f[R] attribute of the given element.
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.side\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R] \f[I](non\-standard)\f[R]
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] corresponding to the
\f[CR]side\f[R] attribute of the given element.
Allowed values are specified by the \f[CR]TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_*\f[R]
constants defined on this interface.
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.startOffset\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedLength\f[R] corresponding to the X component of the
\f[CR]startOffset\f[R] attribute of the given element.
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.method\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] corresponding to the
\f[CR]method\f[R] attribute of the given element.
Allowed values are specified by the \f[CR]TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_*\f[R]
constants defined on this interface.
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.spacing\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] corresponding to the
\f[CR]spacing\f[R] attribute of the given element.
Allowed values are specified by the \f[CR]TEXTPATH_SPACINGTYPE_*\f[R]
constants defined on this interface.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]This interface does not provide any specific methods, but
implements those of its parent, \f[CI]SVGTextContentElement\f[I].\f[R]
.SH STATIC PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_UNKNOWN\f[R] (0)
The type is not one of predefined types.
It is invalid to attempt to define a new value of this type or to
attempt to switch an existing value to this type.
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_ALIGN\f[R] (1)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]align\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_STRETCH\f[R] (2)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]stretch\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SPACINGTYPE_UNKNOWN\f[R] (0)
The type is not one of predefined types.
It is invalid to attempt to define a new value of this type or to
attempt to switch an existing value to this type.
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SPACINGTYPE_AUTO\f[R] (1)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]auto\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SPACINGTYPE_EXACT\f[R] (2)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]exact\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_UNKNOWN\f[R] (0)
The type is not one of the predefined types.
It is invalid to attempt to define a new value of this type or to
attempt to switch an existing value to this type.
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_LEFT\f[R] (1)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]left\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_RIGHT\f[R] (2)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]right\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example shows how you can set and get the properties of an
\f[CR]SVGTextPathElement\f[R].
.SS HTML
First we define the SVG and associated CSS to draw a path with text
drawn along it (this is a near\-copy of the SVG in the \f[CR]path\f[R]
attribute topic).
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 100 100\(dq xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq>
  \f[I]<!\-\- to hide the path, it is usually wrapped in a <defs> element \-\->\f[R]
  \f[I]<!\-\- <defs> \-\->\f[R]
  <\f[B]path\f[R]
    id=\(dqMyPath\(dq
    fill=\(dqnone\(dq
    stroke=\(dqred\(dq
    d=\(dqM10,90 Q90,90 90,45 Q90,10 50,10 Q10,10 10,40 Q10,70 45,70 Q70,70 75,50\(dq />

  <\f[B]text\f[R]>
    <\f[B]textPath\f[R] href=\(dq#MyPath\(dq>Quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</\f[B]textPath\f[R]>
  </\f[B]text\f[R]>
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
We also add a button for toggling the \f[CR]side\f[R] property in order
to change what side of the path the text is drawn on.
Note that there is also hidden logging code that is not relevant to the
example.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqtoggleBtn\(dq>Toggle side</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
The code below toggles the \f[CR]side.baseVal\f[R] property on the
\f[CR]textPath\f[R], causing the text to swap sides.
.PP
First we define a function to log each of the properties of the path
element, and call it to log the initial state on load.
The \f[CR]side.baseVale\f[R] property is logged first, and demonstrates
how the enumerated constants may be read and interpreted (this is done
in a \f[CR]try...catch\f[R] block, because \f[CR]side\f[R] is not
supported in all browsers).
The other properties of the text path are also logged, but as raw values
of their associated \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] property.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] textPath = document.querySelector(\(dqtextPath\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] logPathBaseVal() {
  \f[I]// Log the baseVal for each property\f[R]
  log(\(dqLOG:\(dq);

  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[B]let\f[R] side;

    \f[B]if\f[R] (textPath.side.baseVal === SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_RIGHT) {
      side = \(dqright\(dq;
    } \f[B]else\f[R] \f[B]if\f[R] (
      textPath.side.baseVal === SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_LEFT
    ) {
      side = \(dqleft\(dq;
    } \f[B]else\f[R] \f[B]if\f[R] (
      textPath.side.baseVal === SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_UNKNOWN
    ) {
      side = \(dqunknown\(dq;
    } \f[B]else\f[R] {
      side = \(dqunexpected value\(dq;
    }
    log(\(ga Current side: ${side}\(ga);
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] {
    log(\(gaside property is not supported in this browser\(ga);
  }

  log(\(ga href: ${textPath.href.baseVal}\(ga);
  log(\(ga method: ${textPath.method.baseVal}\(ga);
  log(\(ga spacing: ${textPath.spacing.baseVal}\(ga);
  log(\(ga startOffset: ${textPath.startOffset.baseVal}\(ga);
}

\f[I]// Log the initial state on load\f[R]
logPathBaseVal();
.EE
.PP
The toggle button event handler code is shown below This reads the
current value of the \f[CR]side.baseVal\f[R] property, and toggles the
value to match the other side.
It then logs the current state.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Toggle the side when the button is clicked\f[R]
toggleBtn.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (textPath.side.baseVal === SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_RIGHT) {
      \f[I]// Change to left\f[R]
      textPath.side.baseVal = SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_LEFT;
    } \f[B]else\f[R] {
      \f[I]// Change to right\f[R]
      textPath.side.baseVal = SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_RIGHT;
    }

    \f[I]// Log the updated state\f[R]
    logPathBaseVal();
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] (e) {
    log(\(dqSetting the side property is not supported in this browser.\(dq);
  }
});
.EE
.SS Result
Press the button to toggle the states.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]<textPath>\f[R]
